{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792367481,"nonce":"VbnTm6hg3HUBVjxGGpmbwZ2znPs=","message":"**Draft API for the first three items, not built yet**\n\nRayDE's debugger needs a breakpoint dot in the gutter that a click toggles, a full-line background for the line it stopped on or the current match, and inline ranges for diagnostics and hover. One shape for all three, each set owned by a name so a producer replaces its own and leaves the others:\n\n- `editor.decorate(owner:String, list:Array\u003cCodeDecoration\u003e):Void` replaces that owner's decorations; an empty list clears them. `CodeDecoration = {from:Int, to:Int, className:String, ?title:String, ?wholeLine:Bool}`: offsets into the text, as `select` takes them; `wholeLine` ignores the columns and paints the full width of each line the range touches (a stopped line is `{from: lineStart, to: lineStart, wholeLine: true}`). Drawn as elements behind the text for the rows in the window, one per row a range covers, class from the app, so appearance is CSS. The editor ships `ui-code-squiggle-error`, `-warning` and `-info` (a wavy underline in `--ui-code-error`, `--ui-code-warning`, `--ui-code-info`) and `ui-code-line-current`.\n- `editor.markers(owner:String, list:Array\u003cCodeMarker\u003e):Void`, `CodeMarker = {line:Int, className:String, ?title:String}` (line is zero-based, as `toggleFold` takes it): a slot in the gutter left of the line numbers shows an element of that class (a dot by default for `ui-code-marker-breakpoint`; an app puts an icon in with CSS). `editor.onGutterClick = (line, event) -\u003e ...` is called for a press in that slot on any line, with or without a marker, so breakpoints toggle where there are none yet.\n- Hover: `editor.onHover = (offset, rect) -\u003e ...` after a delay, with the character's screen rectangle, and `editor.rectAt(offset)` and `editor.offsetAt(x, y)` for placing popups. That is item 5 and 6 of the list and shares the position lookup.\n\nRows are pooled (b973ba1), so a decoration is bound to the row it covers by the same slot, and only the sets that change redo their elements. Each item gets a check in CodeComponents.","files":null}]}